k6 script used for the report "Leaderboard holds 1,000 concurrent learners":
  export const options = { vus: 1000, duration: "10m" };
  export default function () {
    http.get(`${BASE}/api/leaderboard?courseId=42`);
  }
Result: mean http_req_duration 200 ms.
Product analytics: a learner on the leaderboard page reloads it about every 30 s.

Statement: "Without a sleep() between iterations, these 1,000 VUs send roughly 5,000 requests per second, about 150 times what 1,000 real learners send, so the test measures a much heavier load than its title says."
